  "body": "From the independent review of PR #397 (#316, merged as 13802a1), both non-blocking:\n\n1. `crates/app/src/commands/setup.rs` is 445 lines (was 432 before #397), past the ~400-line law. Suggested seam: move `DeleteSetup` and its guards (the \"another setup is linked to it\" refusal) into `commands/setup_delete.rs`.\n2. No test pins that a child setup's generated toolpaths go stale when the parent's alignment change re-places the child (it works today only because the operation stamp includes the setup's part alignment). Add a test in `crates/app/tests/setup_relative.rs`: generate an op in a linked child, change the parent's alignment, assert the child op is Stale; undo -> fresh again.\n\nAlso: a stray blank line in `crates/app/src/commands/setup_align.rs`.\n\n**Done means:** the split lands with no behaviour change (all setup suites green), and the stale test is in and passes.\n",
